WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.267 --> 00:00:10.951
This video shows the stages of a payment, each with its own animated icon. The state of a stage decides whether its icon moves or stands still.

2
00:00:11.500 --> 00:00:19.154
Our checkout lists three stages. The first one is done, so let's give it its icon, standing still on its last frame.

3
00:00:28.200 --> 00:00:35.149
Progress, set to one, shows the end of the animation and holds it there. A finished stage stays calm.

4
00:00:36.367 --> 00:00:40.755
The second stage is running right now, so its icon should move.

5
00:00:50.567 --> 00:00:58.665
Autoplay plays it as the file says, and the file repeats the scan. So it keeps scanning while the stage runs.

6
00:00:59.900 --> 00:01:06.404
The last stage has not started yet. Let's show its icon half way, without motion.

7
00:01:16.300 --> 00:01:25.600
Progress, set to a half, shows the middle of the animation, and the style for the next stage fades it. Only the running stage draws the eye.

8
00:01:26.833 --> 00:01:36.368
So, one component shows every stage. Progress holds a still frame for the stages that wait or are done, and autoplay moves the one that runs.
